<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Weald</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Weald is an area of south-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> between the North and South Downs, covering parts of Kent, Sussex, Surrey and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hampshire">Hampshire</a>. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> times it was a great forest, Andredesweald, that separated the South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> from their neighbours and was used mainly for seasonal pasture. From Roman times to the 18th century it was also an important iron-producing district.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/the-weald.jpg" alt="The Weald" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Rjgibb · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WealdfromDowns.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
